David Hairston queries:
> just what is a grid bug?

Jeff d'Arcy responds:
> Grid bugs are the nasties from ChipWits, an amusing and somewhat educational
> game that ran on early Macintoshen.  The object was to program a little robot
> (in a pictorial language called IBOL) to navigate a maze, pick up objects and
> zap grid bugs.

NetHack's grid bugs were based on Tron.  Grid bugs appear briefly in
the movie (probly a cut scene), and populate a stage of the video
game.  These long-legged electrical bugs walk along grid lines.  In
NetHack, they walk on the floor, but their movement is uniquely
restricted.  In the video game, they danced about in troops, making
space to divide into more bugs, but NetHack's grid bugs just come in
small groups.  They're pretty wimpy, one hit usually derezzes them.


